Aether: dead callsites, part A

ExtensionTelemetry, Nimbus, autofill, startup, BrowserUsage, WebRTC emitter, telemetry events, translations, usage calls, AboutWelcome.

Squashed from 14 units:

  [core/36-dead-exttelemetry-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead extension telemetry call sites
  
  An earlier patch emptied the bodies of ExtensionTelemetry's metric objects, so
  every call to them became a no-op that still paid for a lazy module load, a
  Proxy lookup and an allocation per call. The callers were left behind.
  
  This removes the calls and everything that existed only to feed them:
  
  * the GIFFT mirror loop in ext-backgroundPage.js, which repeated a categorical
    histogram add because the format cannot mirror a value other than 1, and
    with it the label list, the timing read and the surrounding if;
  * the suspend counter and its TODO, which wanted a service-worker equivalent;
  * measureOp in ext-storage.js, a helper whose whole body was start, finish
    and cancel, and with it the two storage call sites that went through it;
  * the lazy import-map entries that pointed at the metric objects.
  
  ExtensionTelemetry.sys.mjs keeps only getTrimmedString, which
  ExtensionStorageIDB still needs to bound extension ids and error names.
  getErrorNameForTelemetry had no callers left at all and goes with the rest.
  
  [core/37-dead-nimbus-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead NimbusTelemetry call sites
  
  Six of NimbusTelemetry's methods were already empty shells: recording
  enrollment failures, exposures, migrations, Remote Settings sync errors,
  unenrollment failures and validation failures did nothing. Their thirteen
  call sites stayed behind across ExperimentManager, the Remote Settings
  experiment loader, the migrations runner and the experiment API.
  
  This removes the calls. The live half of the module stays: recordEnrollment,
  recordUnenrollment, recordEnrollmentStatus and setExperimentActive manage
  experiment state (not pings), and the eight reason/status enums are still
  used by the callers, so no import line changes.
  
  Per-site notes: the exposure flag write in ExperimentAPI stays because the
  once-only dedup reads it; the migrations runner loses the duration timing
  and the reason classification that only fed the metric; two single-statement
  ifs and one for-loop go whole rather than leaving empty blocks.
  
  [core/38-dead-autofill-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead AutofillTelemetry module and its call sites
  
  The module was a dispatch chain (static facade, per-type instances, extra
  object builders) whose every terminal method was empty: recording a form
  event, a doorhanger event, a manage event, a profile count or a submission
  heuristic count did nothing. Its twenty-one call sites stayed behind across
  the section tracker, the doorhanger prompter, the child actor, the storage
  base and the two management dialogs.
  
  This removes the calls and, with the last importer gone, the module itself
  with its EXTRA_JS_MODULES entry. The extra builders and the iframe-layout and
  cc-number counters only existed to feed the empty terminals, so they go with
  the chain rather than leaving dead computation behind.
  
  Tests: the dynamic-form telemetry test asserted live Glean values and must
  fail with nothing recorded, so it is deleted with its manifest entry. The iOS
  library test and the address dialog test keep their functional flows; only the
  telemetry stub, its assertions and the expected-args scaffolding are removed.
  The iframe-layout and passport tests had their asserts emptied by earlier
  patches and need nothing.
  
  [core/39-dead-startup-module.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead StartupTelemetry module
  
  The whole module was dead weight: five empty telemetry methods plus initFOG
  and aiControlBlocking, neither of which has a single caller anywhere in the
  tree. Its only wiring was two manifest category lines for idle-startup hooks
  whose bodies did nothing, and the moz.build entry.
  
  This deletes the module, its manifest lines (the categories keep all their
  other registrants) and its build entry. It also fixes a stale comment in
  PlacesDBUtils that still claimed its telemetry hook was called by
  StartupTelemetry: the caller was removed by an earlier patch, so the comment
  lied.
  
  [core/40-dead-btu-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead BrowserTelemetryUtils call and module
  
  TabsProgressListener.onStateChange carried a block that collected tab load
  times: a metric classification, per-browser timer fields and a recording call
  whose method body was already empty. Everything in that block existed only for
  the metric, so the whole block goes rather than leaving timer state written
  onto every browser object on every page load. onStateChange stays as an
  (empty) listener method.
  
  With its only call gone, the single-method module is deleted with its
  moz.build entry and its lazy import-map line.
  
  [core/41-webrtc-no-emitter.patch]
  Aether: cut webrtcUI off the unpackaged EventEmitter
  
  The Sync wipe dropped the syncedtabs dir from the build, so its EventEmitter
  module is never staged and never reaches omni.ja - while webrtcUI.sys.mjs
  imported it at its top level. The first page to touch WebRTC then died
  loading the module, which can break the camera/microphone permission flow.
  
  WebRTCParent emits peer-request-allowed/blocked/cancel through
  webrtcUI.emitter, so the property is load-bearing even though nothing in
  shipped code subscribes. This replaces the unpackaged import with a small
  local emitter class of the same on/off/emit shape, defined in webrtcUI
  itself, and on/off delegate to it again. No build files change: the dir
  stays out of the build as the Sync wipe intended.
  
  [core/42-dead-telemetry-events.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead normandy TelemetryEvents module and its call sites
  
  TelemetryEvents.sendEvent was already an empty method, so its thirteen call
  sites across the add-on studies, preference experiments and preference
  rollouts code recorded nothing. They go with the lazy import-map lines and,
  with the last importer gone, the eight-line module itself (no build file ever
  listed it).
  
  Tests: the head.js spy helper becomes an identity decorator and every
  spy-dependent assertion goes with it (assertEvents blocks, call counts,
  getCall reads, the AddonStudies snapshotEvents block). Destructured spy
  params stay, binding undefined harmlessly. Functional enrollment flows and
  their asserts are untouched.
  
  [core/43-translations-telemetry-sink.patch]
  Aether: no-op sink for TranslationsParent.telemetry()
  
  An earlier patch removed the telemetry method but left some forty
  fire-and-forget call sites across the two translation panels, so every panel
  interaction threw TypeError. This adds the method back as a sink: a Proxy
  that returns itself for any property get and any call, absorbing every
  existing chain shape with no recording. Patch 04 owns the original removal;
  this only repairs the call sites it left behind.
  
  [core/44-dead-usage-calls-1.patch]
  Aether: remove dead BrowserUsageTelemetry calls, part 1
  
  Done in four verified parts so the big module does not break halfway:
  
  1. the single recordInteractionEvent call (empty-bodied method) in the
     all-tabs menu, with its now-unused import;
  2. the widgetMap chain: 23 recordWidgetChange/recordToolbarVisibility calls
     plus the internal map maintenance (_recordWidgetChange, _recordUITelemetry,
     _buildWidgetPositions) that nothing outside the module reads;
  3. the tab-counter chain: counter methods, state, helpers, throttle const and
     pref getter, with the counter lines inside functional handlers removed and
     the handlers themselves intact;
  4a. the two reportInstallationTelemetry calls (empty method, return unused).
  
  Explicitly deferred (part 4b): ignoreEvent and the _recordCommand pipeline.
  That pipeline still writes functional prefs (browser.engagement.*.used-count
  and .has-used) that other features read, so removing it changes product
  behavior rather than just deleting dead code. It belongs with the legacy
  system demolition, once what reads those prefs is audited.
  
  [core/45-dead-aboutwelcome-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead AboutWelcomeTelemetry call sites
  
  The module is eight lines with a single empty method, but three shipped files
  wired into it, one hiding a live crash: ASRouterTelemetry called
  parseAndSubmitPing on the instance, which does not exist there, so every
  ASRouter telemetry user event threw TypeError. Spotlight routed one call
  through its default dispatch, and AboutWelcomeParent sent session-end and page
  events into the void.
  
  This removes the three calls with their imports and lazy getters. The
  AWPage:TELEMETRY_EVENT case keeps its break (the message is handled by
  ignoring it), Spotlight keeps its dispatch routing and its default-dispatch
  method, and ASRouterTelemetry keeps building its pings (demolishing that
  system is larger work, not this unit). The module file itself stays until its
  test importers are reviewed separately.
  
  [core/46-dead-newtab-doh-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead NewTabUtils and DoH telemetry leftovers
  
  Two small units with the same shape: machinery whose recording end is gone.
  
  NewTabUtils carried a local Telemetry singleton that observed idle-daily only
  to call an empty _collect. The singleton, its init/uninit calls and the topic
  const nothing else uses go together.
  
  DoHController kept an empty for-loop over heuristic names whose body an
  earlier patch removed, spinning over nothing at init. DoHHeuristics kept a
  fromResults mapper with no callers and a result-code object that only it used
  (the object itself says it mirrors removed Scalars and Glean metrics). Both
  go; the DISABLE_DOH decision logic and everything else stays.
  
  [core/47-dead-search-calls.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead BrowserSearchTelemetry calls
  
  Every method on the module is an empty body (verified by reading it whole),
  so its seventeen call sites recorded nothing. They go, with the import lines
  left without references. The shared KNOWN_SEARCH_SOURCES map and the
  shouldRecordSearchCount predicate stay: other modules reference the map and
  the predicate gates behavior, and both need their own analysis.
  
  Careful bits: UrlbarParentController.recordSearch does functional work
  (search-count prefs, the ASRouter trigger, form history), so only its inner
  dead call goes and the rest stands. Its recordSearchMode/Form wrappers did
  nothing else and become empty methods, which must exist because actor
  messages and direct callers still address them. The searchbar tab-open
  conditional recorded on both branches, so the whole conditional goes.
  SportsFeed only mentioned the call in a comment, reworded.
  
  The module itself and the 2175-line SearchSERPTelemetry engine stay: the
  engine is a subsystem demolition of its own, not call-site cleanup.
  
  [core/48-dead-usage-calls-2.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead BrowserUsageTelemetry calls, part 2
  
  The tab-counter chain (counter methods, state, helpers, throttle const and
  pref getter) and the widgetMap chain (23 calls, the map maintenance, the
  builders) only fed recording that no longer happens. The two
  reportInstallationTelemetry calls go with them; the ping building stays.
  
  AboutWelcomeParent: the AboutWelcomeTelemetry singleton is an empty
  sendTelemetry, so its two calls and the lazy getter go. The
  AWPage:TELEMETRY_EVENT case keeps its break (the message is handled by
  ignoring it). The telemetryEnabledPref getter stays (gates behavior).
  
  [core/49-legacy-callsites.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead legacy-telemetry call sites
  
  Product code still reached into nsITelemetry for clocks, gates
  and payload plumbing whose recording side is long gone:
  the language-preference telemetryId chain, the empty
  recordTelemetry shells, PurgeTrackerService's prerelease gates
  and write-only last_purge pref, the BHR telemetry service
  (never shipped: nightly-gated), the background-page creation
  timestamp, the login autocomplete telemetryEventData, the
  devtools timer wrappers, the GIFFT mirrors in all Glean
  counter/event/timing bindings (fog_ calls kept; the
  timing-distribution FFI shells stay as no-ops until the
  Rust callers go), the test-only telemetry IPC probes
  (RDD/utility/socket) and the socket-process ping chain, the
  empty media-codec reporter calls and the startup IO-reporting
  hooks. All removed; functional behavior (purge logic,
  autocomplete fill messages, devtools timers via local
  clocks) preserved. The backend itself goes in the follow-up.
